{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017zdzb7EEo91diE3x6kznD4","type":"tool_result","content":"    30→\n    31→# Words that indicate character context\n    32→CHARACTER_VERBS = {\n    33→    'said', 'asked', 'replied', 'whispered', 'shouted', 'muttered',\n    34→    'thought', 'wondered', 'felt', 'looked', 'smiled', 'laughed',\n    35→    'walked', 'ran', 'stood', 'sat', 'turned', 'nodded',\n    36→}\n    37→\n    38→\n    39→VALIDATION_SYSTEM_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are a literary analyst validating character names.\n    40→\n    41→Your task is to determine if a proposed name refers to a real character (person) in the story,\n    42→and identify other names that might refer to the same person.\n    43→\n    44→Consider:\n    45→- Is this a person's name (not a place, title alone, or abstract concept)?\n    46→- Does the context suggest this is a character who acts, speaks, or is spoken about?\n    47→- What other names/titles might refer to the same person?\"\"\"\n    48→\n    49→\n    50→VALIDATION_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = \"\"\"Validate this character proposal from a novel:\n    51→\n    52→PROPOSED NAME: {name}\n    53→STRATEGY: {strategy}\n    54→MENTION COUNT: {mention_count}\n    55→\n    56→SAMPLE CONTEXTS (where this name appears):\n    57→{contexts}\n    58→\n    59→Please analyze and return JSON with:\n    60→- \"is_person\": true/false - Is this a real person/character name (not a place, title, or concept)?\n    61→- \"is_person_reasoning\": Brief explanation\n    62→- \"context_supports\": 0.0-1.0 - How strongly does the context support this being a character?\n    63→- \"alias_candidates\": List of other names that might refer to the same person (e.g., \"Elizabeth\" -> [\"Lizzy\", \"Miss Bennet\"])\n    64→- \"overall_valid\": true/false - Should we include this as a character?\n    65→\n    66→Return ONLY valid JSON.\"\"\"\n    67→\n    68→\n    69→class CharacterValidator:\n    70→    \"\"\"\n    71→    Validates character proposals using heuristics and LLM.\n    72→\n    73→    Uses fast heuristics for clear cases, LLM for ambiguous ones.\n    74→    \"\"\"\n    75→\n    76→    def __init__(\n    77→        self,\n    78→        llm_client: Optional[LLMClient] = None,\n    79→        min_confidence: float = 0.5,\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6051e2-acb8-49c7-9168-f3c046842986","uuid":"ac43d08e-b5fa-4576-972f-6a89616ef0e1","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/src/pipeline/character_extraction/validator.py","content":"\n# Words that indicate character context\nCHARACTER_VERBS = {\n    'said', 'asked', 'replied', 'whispered', 'shouted', 'muttered',\n    'thought', 'wondered', 'felt', 'looked', 'smiled', 'laughed',\n    'walked', 'ran', 'stood', 'sat', 'turned', 'nodded',\n}\n\n\nVALIDATION_SYSTEM_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are a literary analyst validating character names.\n\nYour task is to determine if a proposed name refers to a real character (person) in the story,\nand identify other names that might refer to the same person.\n\nConsider:\n- Is this a person's name (not a place, title alone, or abstract concept)?\n- Does the context suggest this is a character who acts, speaks, or is spoken about?\n- What other names/titles might refer to the same person?\"\"\"\n\n\nVALIDATION_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = \"\"\"Validate this character proposal from a novel:\n\nPROPOSED NAME: {name}\nSTRATEGY: {strategy}\nMENTION COUNT: {mention_count}\n\nSAMPLE CONTEXTS (where this name appears):\n{contexts}\n\nPlease analyze and return JSON with:\n- \"is_person\": true/false - Is this a real person/character name (not a place, title, or concept)?\n- \"is_person_reasoning\": Brief explanation\n- \"context_supports\": 0.0-1.0 - How strongly does the context support this being a character?\n- \"alias_candidates\": List of other names that might refer to the same person (e.g., \"Elizabeth\" -> [\"Lizzy\", \"Miss Bennet\"])\n- \"overall_valid\": true/false - Should we include this as a character?\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass CharacterValidator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates character proposals using heuristics and LLM.\n\n    Uses fast heuristics for clear cases, LLM for ambiguous ones.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        llm_client: Optional[LLMClient] = None,\n        min_confidence: float = 0.5,","numLines":50,"startLine":30,"totalLines":378}}}
